# A reference trick: the running walking policy (sar_walk) is fed this joint-offset
# reference once, the same way the joystick's game mode triggers its jump. Only
# policies trained with this reference can follow it; the default policy was.
# The table is the one the game player uses too (pupper/references/jump.json).
#
# Off by default. To let Gemini jump on request, rename this file to trick.yaml.
description: Jumps straight up in place and lands standing. Only when the user clearly asks for a jump, with clear space around the robot.
type: reference
reference: ../../../pupper/references/jump.json
start_pose: standing
end_pose: standing
